SUMMARY:Raj Se Swaraj Tak From Colonial Rule to Freedom- Through the Eyes
  of Shekhawati
LOCATION:Visual Arts Gallery\, India Habitat Centre\, Lodhi Road\, New De
 lhi 110003
URL:https://indiahabitat.org/Exhibitions_Details
DESCRIPTION:To mark India’s 80th year of Independence\, MOHAR (Museum o
 f Heritage and Art at Ramgarh) presents “Raj Se Swaraj Tak”\, an imme
 rse eight-day journey of pre-independence and Post independence India in 
 the 1800s and 1900s\, through the discoveries in the Havelies of the Shek
 hawati Seths\, who created the magical frescoed region of Shekhawati\, ca
 lled the “Open-air Art gallery of Rajasthan”.\nThe exhibition and oth
 er events will showcase cultural narratives and lifestyles through the wa
 ll frescoes of Shekhawati\, the art and design influences\, belief system
 s\, religious and folk stories\, the British influence\, political art\, 
 lifestyle secrets\, architecture\, attire\, objects created or acquired b
 y the Shekhawati Seths - Art\, Media\, Manuscripts\, Telegrams\, Newspape
 rs\, Letters\, Maps\, spectacular oleographs\,\n\nhttps://indiahabitat.or
 g/Exhibitions_Details
CATEGORIES:exhibition\,art\,history
END:VEVENT
